> > This field is derived dynamically within the Flink app (as it depends on the data flowing through the app)
>
> How do you send the dynamically collected data to the `func`? The function is serialized during the job creation, and then sent to the committer. When the committer is started, then the function is deserialized and executed, but only already serialized information, and information available in the committer could be used by the function.

Great point. In prototype, we stored the min/max event time in a static variable and accessed it within `func`. Since the operator is a global reducer, both the operator and the committer were always scheduled in the same JVM and it can be accessed. For larger scale cases, we can store it in external storage (e.g. memcached, S3) and access it there.

```
.setSnapshotPropertyGenerator((checkpointId) -> {
    Stats stats = S3Client.readStatsForCheckpoint(checkpointId);
    return generateIcebergSnapshotProperties(stats);
});
```
But I agree this approach is a bit limited, and I’d like to take a step back and research the best way to propagate necessary metadata to the committer, so we can reliably set dynamic snapshot properties at chec […]
